      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَحَاحٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِحَّةٌ</span>, in two places: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  and see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَحِيحٌ</span>, in four places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَحَاحُ الطَّرِيقِ</span> means
(assumed tropical:)  <i>The hard part of the road, that has not been
rendered soft,</i> or <i>plain,</i> (K, TA,) <i>nor smooth,</i> or
<i>easy to walk or ride upon.</i> (TA.)

